    "resizing": {
        "planning_paired_items_per_probe_type": 150,
        "source_tier": "M",
        "rule": "For each probe type t, n_t = ceil(DE_t * ((z_a * sqrt(d_t) + z_b * sqrt(d_t - e_t^2)) / e_t)^2), where d_t is the paired discordance observed at M, floored at e_t because a paired difference of e_t needs discordance of at least e_t, so the term under the root stays non-negative when M observes little or no discordance; e_t is the family's registered L mde for superiority families and its 10 pp margin for noninferiority families, each divided by 100 so that e_t is a proportion on the same scale as d_t; z_a is z(1 - alpha/2) for superiority and z(1 - alpha/5) for the five Holm-corrected harm metrics, the Holm first step; z_b is z(0.8), the target power for every family (the harm family's registered power records what its planning count reaches, so it is an input to no re-sizing), with the variance term sqrt(d_t) in place of sqrt(d_t - e_t^2) for noninferiority families, whose power is planned at a true difference of 0; and DE_t = 1 + (m_t - 1) * ICC_t is the design effect over ledger_fact_id clusters, with m_t the mean paired items per fact and ICC_t estimated at M. L's paired_items_per_probe_type becomes max_t n_t and is recorded before the first L run."
    },
    "load_stress": {
